NONE","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\nv4.6.rc2.official [78c6632eb]\n\n### System information\n\nGodot v4.6.rc2 - Windows 11 (build 26200) - Multi-window, 2 monitors - Direct3D 12 (Forward+) - dedicated NVIDIA GeForce RTX 2060 (NVIDIA; 32.0.15.8180) - AMD Ryzen 5 3600 6-Core Processor (12 threads) - 15.88 GiB memory\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen alt-dragging a TextFile from the FileSystem into the Script window, an `@export` variable is created with the \"TextFile\" type annotation even though \"TextFile\" isn't a valid type, causing the script to raise an error.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a text file and a script anywhere in your project.\n2. Hold alt and drag the text file from the FileSystem dock into the script window to create an export variable from the file.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\nIssue is simple enough to reproduce that an MRP seems redundant.","closed_by":{"login":"kitbdev","id":10054226,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEwMDU0MjI2","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/10054226?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev","html_url":"https://github.com/kitbdev","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_eve